(HOW IT WORKS) 700 kicker
/HB 25 F LM 674 moveto (How a print job runs a language model) show

/wfR /TR def /wsz 12 def /wld 15.6 def
(TONER-1 is the most capable language model ever to run entirely inside a print job.* It is one 595~KB PostScript file. Send it to a laser printer and the printer's own processor writes a short story, usually about a printer, then prints it. The computer that sent it does no math.)
LM 649 470 wrap
/p1y wy def

% ---------- three ideas ----------
/colw 156 def /colg 18 def
/ct p1y 28 sub def
[ (01) (A print job is a program)
  (PostScript, the language most laser printers speak, is not a file format but a complete programming language, stack-based like Forth. Send `3 `4 `add and the interpreter leaves 7 on its stack. It has variables, loops and floating-point math. A print job is simply a program; the printed page is a side effect of the drawing commands it calls.)
  (02) (Printers are computers)
  (To run those programs, every PostScript printer carries its own processor and memory. The 1985 Apple LaserWriter had a 12~MHz Motorola 68000 and 1.5~MB of RAM, a faster CPU than the original Macintosh it plugged into (a 68000 at about 7.8~MHz). Modern printers have far more, and spend most of it waiting for spreadsheets.)
  (03) (An LLM is just arithmetic)
  (Strip away the mystique and a language model is a long list of multiplications and additions: matrix-vector products, a normalization step, a softmax that turns scores into probabilities, and a weighted coin flip that picks the next word piece. Any language with loops and multiplication can run one. PostScript has both.)
] /cols exch def
/colbot ct def
0 1 2 { /c exch def
  /cx0 LM c colw colg add mul add def
  cx0 cx0 colw add ct 1 hline
  cx0 ct 14 sub moveto 0.4 setgray /HB 7.5 F cols c 3 mul get 1 tshow 0 setgray
  /wfR /HB def /wsz 10.5 def /wld 13 def
  cols c 3 mul 1 add get cx0 ct 29 sub colw wrap
  /wfR /TR def /wfC /CR def /wsz 9.4 def /wld 12.4 def
  cols c 3 mul 2 add get cx0 wy 15 sub colw wrap
  wy colbot lt { /colbot wy def } if
} for

